SUMMARY:Loudon County — data-center moratorium hearing
DESCRIPTION:The Commission will hear a resolution extending the temporary m
 oratorium on data centers/facilities and consider it for a vote in the Com
 mission meeting that follows. Check the agenda\, speaking rules and any ch
 anges before travel.\nProceeding: loudon-2026-moratorium-extension\nAgency
 : Loudon County Commission\nProject phase: Policy hearing on a proposed mo
 ratorium extension\; not an individual facility permit\nRecord status: act
 ive\nOfficial source: https://loudoncounty-tn.gov/public-hearing-12-7-26/\
 nSource checked: 2026-11-18\nAll-day calendar marker for the listed date\,
  not a verified closing clock time. Confirm the clock time\, time zone\, e
 xtensions and submission rules with the agency.\nThe county announcement s
 tates 6 p.m.\; its calendar lists 6–8 p.m. Neither explicitly names a ti
 me zone. The export is date-only: confirm the local start time\, venue and
  speaking procedure before attending. No phone access or speaker-registrat
 ion deadline is verified here.\nOfficial participation instructions: https
 ://loudoncounty-tn.gov/public-hearing-12-7-26/\nFind and review the record
 s: https://clinical-trials.github.io/datacenter/site/?proceeding=tn-loudon
 -moratorium-hearing&prepare=records#citizen\nPrepare a public comment: htt
 ps://clinical-trials.github.io/datacenter/site/?proceeding=tn-loudon-morat
 orium-hearing&prepare=comment#citizen\nCalendar reminders are personal pre
 paration prompts\, not legal filing deadlines. All-day reminder timing fol
 lows the recipient calendar time zone\; confirm settings after adding. Rec
 heck the official notice before acting.
